<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.7 PCT IN APRIL 1-20-NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.7 PCT IN APRIL 1-20-NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by</p>
<p>2.35 billion zlotys, or 1.7 percent, in April 1-20 to 143.87</p>
<p>billion after a 2.2 pct rise in the whole  of March,</p>
<p>preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 6.0 percent in the January-April 20</p>
<p>period against 7.8 percent in the same period of last year.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		  APRIL 1-20   MARCH  APRIL 1-20</p>
<p>									  1996</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		1.7	2.2	 1.6</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   143.87   141.51    112.38</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	25.31    25.00     21.15</p>
<p>  National currency		     118.55   116.51     91.23</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    24.79    24.59     20.73</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    88.99    87.83     60.41</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
